TITLE:: CompositionChip
SUMMARY:: Nested chip for one composed sequence in the Arranger.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/Arranger, Classes/BorderView, Classes/PatternStructure, Classes/Sequencer

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::CompositionChip:: is a LINK::Classes/BorderView:: that LINK::Classes/Arranger:: places for a LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-compose:: sequence. The title is the sequence id. The title text passes mouse events to the chip. Dragging the title moves the whole chip and calls LINK::#-dragAction_:: with the chip's origin. A click on the title selects that id. A double-click on the title plays it, or stops it when that id is already playing. The body is laid out from a LINK::Classes/PatternStructure::. LINK::Classes/Ppar:: and LINK::Classes/Pchain:: stack their children. Other list patterns lay children out in a row. A repeat count other than 1 is drawn on the label. Nested chips do not drag. A nested chip with a sequence id selects and plays that id. An anonymous chip selects and plays the nearest sequence that contains it. LINK::#-applyPlaying:: highlights this chip when its id is playing, and highlights each nested chip whose id is playing.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::CompositionChip:: and adds it to CODE::parent::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The LINK::Classes/View:: that holds the chip.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: that plays this chip's sequence.

ARGUMENT:: sequenceId
The LINK::Classes/Symbol:: drawn as the title.

ARGUMENT:: structure
The LINK::Classes/PatternStructure:: drawn in the body.

ARGUMENT:: selectAction
A LINK::Classes/Function:: called with the LINK::Classes/Symbol:: to select.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::CompositionChip:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: applyPlaying
Sets this chip's border, and the border of each nested chip, from CODE::playingId::.

ARGUMENT:: playingId
The LINK::Classes/Symbol:: currently playing, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: dragAction_
Called with the chip's origin when a drag of the title is released. CODE::nil:: clears it.

ARGUMENT:: action
A LINK::Classes/Function:: or CODE::nil::. The function receives one LINK::Classes/Point::.

METHOD:: moveTo
Moves the chip so its top-left is CODE::origin::.

ARGUMENT:: origin
A LINK::Classes/Point::.

METHOD:: sequenceId
The sequence LINK::Classes/Symbol:: drawn as the title.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Symbol::.

PRIVATE:: prBuild, prInit, prLayout, prPlace, prTogglePlay, prWire, prWireFrame
